{"kind":"assert","text":"Security finding on child 676249f0: the landed host API can satisfy the no-server-key boundary without a core change, but candidate 2bbbb4b has a second proof-boundary defect. /github/start accepts a raw actor public key without proof of possession. A same-origin caller can therefore ask the deployment witness to bind that caller's GitHub identity to another actor key; if the target is or later becomes seated, the attacker's identity can gain recovery authority. The repair must require a bounded one-shot browser challenge and Ed25519 possession signature before OAuth state/provider access, with a mutation test that fails when verification is removed or the key/signature is changed. For witness custody, chess serve must expose no private-key field, key loader, witness-key environment variable, or identity.Endorse call. It prepares the existing identity anchor, sends only PreparedAct to a separately custodied signer, receives only public key plus signature over host.ActorSigningBytes, checks the current declared witness key, and appends through AppendSigned. No token, authorization code, PKCE verifier, state, or client secret may cross that signer boundary. Without a real external signer, Witnessed GitHub anchoring is impossible under the existing fold."}